+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The directive may be used at module level or inside
+   a class. Its optional body can describe the alias. The alias does not
+   establish a nesting context for objects described in its body.
+
+   The optional ``canonical`` option describes the type represented by the
+   alias. When provided, it is shown after the alias name with an equals sign,
+   and its annotation is parsed so that type references can be resolved.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Describe the type represented by this alias.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
